 "show": "deadmau5 - Strobe (Dimension Remix)",
 "about": "Bars of the analysis grid: bar b starts at 1.037 + 1.379 b seconds, 224 bars, 174 BPM. The analysis puts its bar line one beat early: the kick, every entry, both drops and every phrase restart land on its beat two, so every mark here sits at .25, a beat past the grid's downbeat. Strobe's own language comes back -- the same sixteen-spark constellation (loop 16, seed 3) whenever the melody is alone, ice for the climb, dawn for the second breakdown, the strobe palette under the drops, the ladder, the spin, the ring, the X eyes -- and the remix adds its own: the two-step breakbeat played on the ears, the kick on both ears' tubes on 1 and the and-of-3, the snare in hot volt pink on the left half and ear 1 on beat 2, answered by the right half and ear 2 on beat 4. Every phrase restart has a one-beat hole in the bass before it, and the helmet goes dark for exactly that beat. The kick runs the tubes at under half and the snares at 0.6 on purpose: a full-bright ear flash takes the whole 1000 mA and the governor sheds the shell at s^6, which left the snare halves dark on the face. Nothing on the shell, and no pump, pulses faster than a beat (2.9 Hz); only the ear blades go to 8ths, and to 16ths for single bars before a restart. White once, on drop 2.",
